    <div class="section" id="method">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-head section-head--center">
                <h2>Judge First, Then Adjust</h2>
                <p>Break feng shui problems into executable, reviewable, verifiable steps</p>
            </div>
            <div class="process">
                <div class="process-step">
                    <div class="process-num">1</div>
                    <div class="process-title">Identify Problem Type</div>
                    <div class="process-desc">First identify entry, bedroom, kitchen, office or naming issues, avoid piling up solutions at once.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="process-step">
                    <div class="process-num">2</div>
                    <div class="process-title">Start with Low-Cost Items</div>
                    <div class="process-desc">Prioritize flow, lighting, storage and buffer zones, do high-impact low-rework actions first.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="process-step">
                    <div class="process-num">3</div>
                    <div class="process-title">Then Move to Deep Consultation</div>
                    <div class="process-desc">When you need floor plan analysis, on-site assessment or long-term tracking, upgrade to 1:1 consultation or deep analysis.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="process-step">
                    <div class="process-num">4</div>
                    <div class="process-title">Weekly Review Results</div>
                    <div class="process-desc">Change only one variable per week, record sleep, focus, spending and progress speed, judge if adjustments are effective.</div>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>

