    <div class="section" id="home-faq">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Feng Shui Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                <p>Start with low-cost high-impact actions, then decide whether to proceed with deep consultation.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-list">
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <div class="faq-q">Does an unfavorable door direction directly cause wealth stagnation？</div>
                    <div class="faq-a"><p>Not necessarily. Direction is just one condition，Usually more critical is entry flow、lighting and storage whether allow space“come in and stay”。Suggest first do entry cleanup and lighting optimization，then observe 7-14 days changes。</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <div class="faq-q">When budget is limited, which feng shui adjustment should be done first?</div>
                    <div class="faq-a"><p>Prioritize the 1-2 most impactful issues：Entry area messy, bedroom sleep area unstable, kitchen door stove direct clash。First stabilize these high-impact items，Usually more effective than one major change。</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <div class="faq-q">Is it worth optimizing feng shui for a rental property?</div>
                    <div class="faq-a"><p>Worth it. Rentals are more suitable for reversible, low-cost actions，Such as flow adjustment, lighting layering, soft partitions and storage optimization，Execute fast, low trial-and-error cost。</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <div class="faq-q">How long after adjustment is best to review？</div>
                    <div class="faq-a"><p>Suggest review every 7-14 days，Record sleep, focus, emotions and task progress efficiency。After 4 consecutive weeks of review, decide whether to upgrade plan。</p></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

